SUMMARY:Rapp Lecture on Contemporary Art: Lotus L. Kang and Ebony L. Hayne
 s (Free)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n( WINNER of the 2026 Sobey Art Award )
 \n\n*The Rapp Lecture on Contemporary Art features distinguished internati
 onal leaders in the contemporary art world\, including artists\, curators\
 , critics\, and scholars. The program was established in 2009 in honour of
  Carol and Morton Rapp.*\n\n***PLEASE reserve your own FREE ticket*** in a
 dvance at the AGO link below.\n\n**Join artist Lotus L. Kang and curator E
 bony L. Haynes as they discuss Kang’s multi-disciplinary creative practi
 ce. They’ll explore how Kang uses unstable and light-sensitive materials
  to consider the relationship between the body and its environments\, and 
 how Haynes’ groundbreaking work leading New York’s 52 Walker Gallery l
 ed to them working together.**\n\nLotus Kang is also short-listed for the 
 upcoming Sobey Art Award. We'll visit her works at the National Gallery in
  Ottawa--on our upcoming trip.\n\nhttps://www.gallery.ca/whats-on/sobey-ar
 t-award\n\n**Lotus L. Kang** is a New York-based artist whose practice spa
 ns sculpture\, photography\, and site-responsive installation. Recent solo
  exhibitions include the Bvlgari Pavilion at the 61st Venice Biennale\, Fr
 ye Art Museum\, 52 Walker\, and Chisenhale Gallery. Her work has also been
  featured in the Whitney Biennial\, Shanghai Biennial\, and New Museum Tri
 ennial\, and is held in major museum collections including the Art Gallery
  of Ontario\, Stedelijk Museum\, Whitney Museum of American Art\, The Gugg
 enheim Museum\, and Museum of Modern Art\, New York.\n\n3 mins intro..\n\n
 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NK00tdA5Qas\n\n**Ebony L. Haynes** is a Ne
 w York-based curator and is the Global Head of Curatorial Projects at Davi
 d Zwirner. She previously led the gallery’s 52 Walker space in Tribeca\,
  NY. Haynes sits on the boards of Artists Space (New York)\, Topical Cream
 \, and the New Art Dealers Alliance. She also runs Black Art Sessions: an 
 online school that offers free professional practice classes to Black stud
 ents worldwide.\n\n**Reserve your own FREE ticket here:**\n\nhttps://ago.c
 a/events/rapp-lecture-contemporary-art-lotus-l.-kang-and-ebony-l.-haynes\n
 \nNote--this ticket gets you into the AGO (for FREE) from 6pm onwards.
