SUMMARY:Roy Thomson Hall: Elmer Iseler Singers Holiday Concert (Reserve FR
 EE ticket)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWe like to attend a holiday concert ea
 ch December.\n\nThis year we'll head to Roy Thomson Hall for a NOON-time c
 oncert on the Friday before Christmas!\n\nDecember 18th ( 11:30am-1pm ) Pe
 rhaps you're off work that day and/or downtown already??!!\n\n# Elmer Isel
 er Singers with Lydia Adams\, conductor and Shawn Grenke\, organist\n\n\\*
 \\*\\****You need to reserve your own FREE ticket*** *through the RTH link
 * I've included below. Signing onto MEETUP is **not** your entry ticket!\n
 \n**The Elmer Iseler Singers\, led by Artistic Director Lydia Adams since 
 1998\, mark their 48th Concert Season in 2026/27. This esteemed 20-voice p
 rofessional ensemble\,** founded by Dr. Elmer Iseler in 1979\, boasts a ri
 ch legacy of captivating audiences locally\, nationally and globally with 
 their exquisite choral performances.\n\nhttps://www.elmeriselersingers.com
 /\n\nWith a focus on Canadian composers\, the JUNO Award-winning group has
  earned acclaim for their diverse repertoire and collaborations with renow
 ned musical partners. Committed to nurturing talent\, they actively suppor
 t emerging singers\, conductors\, and composers through workshops and scho
 larships\, embodying their dedication to artistic excellence and community
  engagement.\n\n**Reserve your ENTRY ticket here--**\n\nhttps://roythomson
 hall.mhrth.com/tickets/elmer-iseler-singers/\n\nFor those interested\, we 
 can meetup in front of Roy Thomson Hall beforehand and sit together. Gener
 al admission seating.
