SUMMARY:Tarragon Theatre:  Call Me By My Cousin's Name (Comedy)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nPlease join us at Tarragon Theatre. Th
 e is the final PREVIEW performance for this upcoming production. On a Sund
 ay afternoon!\n\nTicket link is below. $40\n\nWilliam is an expert on his 
 Persian wife Tara: her mother\, her culture\, her turn-ons. Yet their marr
 iage is collapsing fast. So he plans one last BIG surprise with the help o
 f his infinitely patient colleague Shahriar – who is desperate for a fav
 our of his own. But when Tara’s estranged cousin arrives at the door\, b
 oth women must figure out how to step over the threshold into brave new po
 ssibilities. And not just to escape William’s soggy shrimp.\n\nhttps://t
 arragontheatre.com/plays/tarragon-season-26-27/call-me-by-my-cousins-name/
 \n\nAnahita Dehbonehie’s riotous Diaspora Gothic play is a thrilling exp
 loration of life right now in Iran\, life right now here\, and the space b
 etween who we roleplay and who we long to be—with a shattering immersive
  climax.\n\n### ***“Outside The March is one of Toronto’s top immersiv
 e companies”***\n\n– The Toronto Star\n\n**Ticket link here:** You are
  purchasing for Sunday February 7th (2pm)\n\nhttps://tarragontheatre.com/p
 lays/tarragon-season-26-27/call-me-by-my-cousins-name/
